                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Close Me[/b] is a shy game with simple goals. It is a moving sketchpad of washed out blues and weird red hues. Even the main mechanic of the game is sad. In order to progress the player is forced to exit the game after performing certain tasks. These include rummaging through trash and sleeping. The player character is faceless, but who cares? The only problem with the game's core mechanic is that the player might close the game and never open it again.",
